Mattlikesmen@gmail.com wrote:
> Stuff I have:
> -Amulets of reflection and ESP
> -+2 Excalibur (expert in longsword) and +3 Mjollnir (skilled)
> -Armor: +0 gauntlets of power, +4 small shield, +4 helm of brilliance,
> +2 speed boots, +4 gray dragon scale mail, +0 cloak of displacement.
> Also have a hawaiian shirt, jumping boots, and cloak of protection in
> the bag.  (Which cloak should I use?)

You are in excellent shape for this point in the game.  By the end
you'll want to try to get the weapons to at least +6 and the armor to
+4, but I've won with worse equipment than you have now.  That Hawaiian
Shirt in particular can be helpful, since shirts are so rare and it's
another four or five points of AC enchanted.  Only point you might want
to be aware of is that a Cloak of Displacement has a cancellation of 2
while a Cloak of Protection has a full 3... but being one short of full
cancellation isn't *that* horrible, just be careful around level
drainers.

If you can find a silver shielf, getting that enchanted could help
since then you could swap the amulet of reflection for ESP full time or
life saving.  Life saving would protect you against those unexpected
deaths that just love to wipe out the promising games of people closing
in on their first ascension.


> -Rings of slow digestion, free action conflict, invisibilty,
> levitation, protection from shape changers

Free action is the best.  Slow digestion is actually not too helpful in
the mid and late game, since food becomes so common, can be stuffed
into a blessed bag of holding, and you'll want to keep your stomach not
overfull anyway in order to gain missing resistances.

> -Wands: 6 magic missle and some other damage ones, a few create
> monster, teleport, and one of polymorph

Wands of death are a big thing to work towards, since those will get
you out of lots of bad situations with the Wizard.

> -A bunch of scrolls but nothing especially noteworthy besides one of
> blessed charging.  Once I find some water I'm going to blank them and
> write enchantment scrolls.

You can also blank however many scrolls with one zap of a wand of
cancellation, and it also turns many potion types into water....  Note
that each scroll of magic mapping you save for the mazes will make you
curse that much less once you're there.

> -Spellbooks of force bolt, confuse monster, light, healing, extra
> healing, protection.  (Will I ever be able to cast any of these well or
> should I toss them out?)

Valks don't really need spellbooks so much.  If you find Cone of Cold
(the Valk's special trick) it might be nice.  A spellbook of Magic
Mapping will also be helpful, of course.  Besides that, light can be a
nice convienence.  However, Valks are a definitive melee class, and
keeping on all the armor that makes melee easy makes spellcasting hard.

> -Potions: 5 full healing, some object detection, a couple gain level
> for later, and a bunch of water and junk potions that I will make water
> out of.

Once you reach about level 17, you'll start finding that it becomes
almost impossible to gain additional experience levels through normal
point gains.  It's up to you how long you want to wait to quaff the
potions.  Note that cursed potions of gain level can be useful on the
way up with the Amulet.

> -Other stuff: Blessed bag of holding, blessed touchstone and luckstone,

Careful with the bag around unknown wands (might be cancellation) and
bags (might be tricks or holding [if unID'd]).

> a couple of uncursed magic markers, and an extra blessed magic lamp in
> addition to the one I use as light.  So I guess that means I have one
> wish.

You have a light spell.  You're at a point in the game where I find it
difficult to tell you what to wish for other than multiple wands of
death and one of cancellation.  You might want to erodeproof your armor
and weapons if they're not already.

>  I also have a huge stash of gems that I think is worth about
> 50,000 or so but I can't find any shopkeepers who will buy gems.

There's usually a general store in Minetown.

You definitely should pick up a unicorn horn, and be on the lookout for
wands of digging to help in the mazes.  You also need a lizard corpse
(not a reptile monster, but a "lizard") to keep in your inventory (not
bag), which don't go bad and will halt stoning if eaten.  A blindfold'd
be nice for facing Medusa (your shield might kill her before you get
petrified but why take the chance).  Boots of water walking would
lessen your reliance on fountains and cancellation charges for blanking
and diluting stuff.  Make sure you have fire resistance (Genhennom fire
traps), cold resistance (Baelzebub), poison resistance (you will
eventually regret it if you don't have it) and sleep resistance (ditto,
although free action might help there).  All these can be obtained from
eating the right monsters, and many from getting crowned.

